# Review policy

How to review changes in this repository. It applies to every reviewer, human or AI.

## What matters in this repo

- Behaviour of the job runner in `src/`: retries, ordering, and exit codes.
- `npm test` must pass before merge.

## Raise to review even if small

- `.mergejudge.yml` — the review configuration itself.
- Scheduling or concurrency changes in `src/index.js`.
- Dependency manifest or lockfile changes.

## Block until a human looks

- A removed or weakened permission or authentication check.
- Changes that make failures silent: swallowed errors, dropped exits.

## Ignore

- Formatting; the repo has no formatter config yet, so never relitigate whitespace.
- Lockfile churn generated by tooling.

## Security expectations

- Treat job payloads as untrusted until validated.
- Credentials belong in the environment; never commit keys or `.env*` files.

## Evidence and nits

- Every finding names the file and line and quotes the changed code.
- At most 3 nits per PR.
